   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 1",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b></p><p><span>25th District State Representative; Puyallup School Board, 2015-2023.</span></p><p><br><b>Other Professional Experience</b></p><p><span>Michael served 20 years in the Air Force as an F-16 fighter pilot. He was an instructor pilot, with multiple combat tours, and a squadron commander recognized for his leadership.</span><br><br><b>Education</b></p><p><span>Bachelor of Arts from University of Washington; Masters of Aerospace Sciences from Embry-Riddle Aeronautical University.</span><br><br><b>Community Service</b></p><p><span>Michael served on the Thun Field Advisory Commission, as a volunteer dad for Edgerton Elementary “Watchdogs”, and motivated and taught kids as a coach for a youth basketball team and a Challenger League Baseball team for disabled children.</span><br><br><b>Statement</b></p><p><span>As your representative, Michael kept his word and evaluated every bill based on whether it made our communities safer, more affordable, with more freedom to enjoy life and raise our families. He brought positive solutions, while working across the aisle to pass legislation that will save millions of taxpayer dollars on state capital projects.</span></p><p><span>Michael will continue fighting against the reckless government spending and high taxes that drive up the cost of living for hardworking families. He supports improving public safety, reducing traffic congestion, and strengthening education.&nbsp;</span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">I have more work to do, respectfully asking for your vote ~ Michael&nbsp;</span></em><br>",
