   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><p>David is a Puyallup School District Director, serving since 2021.</p><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><span>Washington State\r\nSchool Directors' Association (WSSDA) Leadership, 2024; Office of the\r\nSuperintendent of Public Instruction Advisory Committee for Gifted Education,\r\n2011&ndash;2021; Washington State Highly Capable Program Technical Working Group,\r\n2010</span><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><p>David is a graduate of the University of Puget Sound, where he earned his BA\r\nin Politics and Government.</p><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><span>Puyallup School\r\nDistrict Volunteer; YMCA Youth Sports Coach; Puyallup PTA Council Legislative\r\nChair; Washington State PTA Region 5 Legislative Chair; Washington State PTA\r\nLegislative Committee; President, Washington Coalition for Gifted Education,\r\n2013&ndash;2021; Northwest Gifted Child Association Board of Directors</span><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><p><span>I am running\r\nto deliver practical solutions for the 25th District. With over two decades of\r\nexperience working for Washington families, I understand that state policy must\r\nprioritize the economic stability of working people. My focus is clear:\r\nstrengthening public education, protecting workers' rights, and expanding\r\neconomic opportunities. I believe in making government work for everyone. I am\r\na school board director and public education advocate committed to being a\r\nresponsive representative who listens to your needs. I would be honored to earn\r\nyour vote for a stronger Washington.</span></p><br/><br/>",
